// =============================================================================
// .aimanager/capsules.local.json - REFERENCE EXAMPLE (capsule values)
// =============================================================================
// This file is the reference example for the LOCAL CAPSULE-VALUES file that
// pairs with the manifest's "capsules" block (technical-considerations 1.11).
// The real file is plain JSON named ".aimanager/capsules.local.json"; this
// documented copy is JSONC so it can explain itself. The values below match the
// "db-preprod" capsule declared in the golden manifest
// (doc/reference-manifest.jsonc).
//
//   - doc/reference-manifest.jsonc    the committed manifest and its "capsules"
//   - doc/technical-considerations.md field shapes (section 1.11)
//   - doc/goal.md                     why a secret value may live here
//
// What this file is:
//   - NEVER committed. It is gitignored and holds real, machine-local values.
//     It is the ONE place a real secret value may sit (technical-considerations
//     1.7 and 5); it is read ONLY inside AI Manager's own process when it runs
//     a capsule, and never reaches the agent, the transcript, or CLI output.
//     It lives outside the personal overlay (.aimanager.local.jsonc) on
//     purpose: the overlay merges into the manifest and is agent-readable,
//     while this file must never be read by the agent.
//   - Scaffolded by "aimanager init": one stub per non-supplied {placeholder}
//     found in the manifest's capsule templates. The developer fills the stubs
//     themselves, out of band; AI Manager never transfers a value.
//
// The committed / local boundary (technical-considerations 1.11):
//   - Whatever the manifest author wrote LITERALLY in a "command" template is
//     committed in the manifest. Every {placeholder} is filled from elsewhere.
//   - Placeholders listed in the capsule's "supplied" are filled by the AGENT
//     at call time (for "db-preprod" that is {query}); they are NOT in this
//     file.
//   - EVERY OTHER placeholder is filled here, by NAME, with a value that is
//     either a literal string OR a "$ENV_VAR" reference.
//
// Each value, independently:
//   - a literal string  -> the real value lives here (this is what softens the
//     "no secret values" non-goal: a literal secret may sit in this file only);
//   - a "$ENV_VAR" ref   -> the value stays in the environment; AI Manager
//     resolves it at run time. Validation checks the reference syntax but does
//     not inspect whether the name currently resolves.
//
// Checks:
//   - "validate local": every non-supplied {placeholder} of every declared
//     capsule has a structurally valid value here.
//   - "doctor": validates the manifest, overlay, and this local configuration
//     together; it does not inspect the environment or any remote service.
//
// Execution (technical-considerations 1.11): argv-based, no shell - each value
// substitutes as one atomic argument, so quotes or $(...) inside a value are
// just data. Both stdout and stderr are scrubbed before returning to the
// agent: every resolved value below is replaced by its {name}.
//
// Run the capsule this file backs:
//   aimanager run db-preprod --query "SELECT id FROM orders LIMIT 5"
// The manifest template is:
//   "mysql -h {host} -u {user} -p{password} {database} -e {query}"
// Every run result displays this declared template, never its resolved form.
// so the non-supplied placeholders filled below are: host, user, password,
// database. {query} is supplied by the agent and is absent here on purpose.
// =============================================================================
{
  // Keyed by capsule name, exactly as declared in the manifest's "capsules".
  "db-preprod": {
    // Non-secret coordinates, kept out of the committed manifest by choice
    // (the author made them {placeholders}); literal values are fine here.
    "host": "db.preprod.acme.example",
    "user": "acme_ro",
    "database": "acme_shop",

    // The secret. Shown here as a "$ENV" reference, which keeps the value in
    // the environment; runtime resolution happens only inside "aimanager run".
    //
    // This value could EQUALLY be a literal secret string, for example
    //   "password": "s3cr3t-preprod-ro"
    // which is the one case where a real secret value may live in a file. Use
    // whichever the team prefers; both are valid, per value.
    "password": "$ACME_PREPROD_DB_PASSWORD"

    // {query} is NOT here: it is "supplied" by the agent at call time.
  }
}
